==========================================
DAY 05 — NETWORKING BASICS
Commands Reference Sheet
Machine: Kali Linux | User: raven
==========================================

--- IP & INTERFACES ---
ip addr show                    # show all interfaces and IP addresses
ip addr show eth0               # show specific interface
hostname -I                     # print all IP addresses (short form)
ip route show                   # show routing table

--- CONNECTIVITY TESTING ---
ping <host>                     # continuous ping (Ctrl+C to stop)
ping -c 4 <host>                # send exactly 4 packets and stop
ping -c 4 google.com            # example: test connectivity to google

--- LISTENING PORTS ---
ss -tuln                        # TCP/UDP listening ports (no process info)
ss -tulnp                       # same, with process names (needs sudo)
ss -t state established         # only established TCP connections
netstat -tuln                   # older alternative to ss (same purpose)

--- DNS LOOKUPS ---
cat /etc/resolv.conf            # DNS servers currently configured
dig <domain>                    # detailed DNS lookup
dig <domain> +short             # just the IP address, no extra details
nslookup <domain>               # simpler DNS lookup tool
host <domain>                   # simplest DNS lookup

--- HTTP REQUESTS WITH CURL ---
curl <url>                      # GET request, prints response body
curl -I <url>                   # headers only (great for checking status codes)
curl -o file.html <url>         # download response to a file
curl -L <url>                   # follow redirects automatically
curl https://api.ipify.org      # find your PUBLIC IP address

--- FINDING SPECIFIC PORT STATUS ---
ss -tuln | grep :22             # check if port 22 (SSH) is listening
ss -tuln | grep :80             # check if port 80 (HTTP) is listening

==========================================
COMMON PORT REFERENCE
==========================================
22    → SSH (remote login)
80    → HTTP (websites)
443   → HTTPS (secure websites)
21    → FTP (file transfer)
3306  → MySQL database
53    → DNS

